{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01D8awodj3MkGApCo2niCG9N","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a **personal productivity + R&D mission-control system** for J.C. Liechty. Grounded claims from the project's own docs:\n\n**Purpose**\n- A single-folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`), stdlib-only Python productivity system that treats **plain markdown files as the source of truth** â€” no database, no syncing, no external dependencies (one declared exception: optional `pywinpty` for terminals).\n\n**What it does â€” the task manager**\n- Tracks tasks across life domains (academic, commercial, family, writing) with a full lifecycle: active â†’ done â†’ cancelled â†’ saved-for-later â†’ restored, stored across `DASHBOARD.md`, `domains/*.md`, `INBOX.md`, `CANCELLED.md`, `SAVED_FOR_LATER.md`.\n- Offers two interfaces over the same markdown: `anchor_gui.py` (a persistent local web dashboard at `localhost:8777`, run as the NSSM Windows service `anchor`) and `anchor.py` (a CLI mirror that also regenerates `dashboard.html`).\n- Self-tests daily at 5 AM via `anchor_healthcheck.py` (parses files, boots a throwaway server, walks every state and the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces fully stubbed), writing `health_reports/`.\n\n**What it ships â€” the R&D control surface (its biggest feature)**\n- A per-project \"cockpit\" for running the **trio** of AI skills â€” researchPrime (Research) â†’ Crucible (Planning) â†’ Foreman (Build) â€” as durable, server-side sessions.\n- Built in four merged generations: v2 (sessions/cached-validated-summaries/grass-ideas/interactive terminal), v3 \"Mission Control\" (real ConPTY terminals, per-session git-worktree isolation, stacking window manager, GWL branding), and v4 \"Project Cockpit\" (one terminal substrate with auto-load-once skill seeding, engine toggle claudeâ†”gemini, inline expanding lane panels with status lights, per-lane doc roles, cost/tokens/time rollups, type-aware deliverable launch).\n- Each lane shows its most-recent session as a tile with one honest status light; clicking expands an inline summary-over-terminal panel â€” launching a session \"feels like a normal Claude Code / Gemini session.\"\n\n**Status**: v4 was built by Foreman (9 waves green, 637 tests passed) and merged to master on 2026-06-13.\n\nOne caveat worth flagging: the git status shows uncommitted changes and several untracked R&D artifacts (`Anchor.md`, `rnd_jobs/`, `.anchor/projects/`, etc.) â€” so the working tree is currently ahead of the last commit. Want me to look into what's pending there?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5b72a27b-802a-4fb9-8994-84613a4d28cc","uuid":"4ba62ec5-0c8f-405d-be26-b1e4e9a40871","request_id":"req_011Cc1JNmtm66RbXyENML6xp"}
